A covector transforms with the inverse Jacobian: $W'_m(y)
 =\frac{\partial x^n}{\partial y^m}W_n(x).$ The gradient of a scalar is the standard example. Applying the chain rule to [eq:scalar-law], $\frac{\partial S}{\partial y^m}
 =\frac{\partial x^n}{\partial y^m}
  \frac{\partial S}{\partial x^n}.$

